{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Forensic Analysis Assumption.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Forensic Analysis Assumption.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"forensic analysis assumption forensic analysis assumption","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Forensic Analysis Assumption.md","fileName":"Forensic Analysis Assumption.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Forensic Analysis Assumption","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 00:47\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Image Authenticity and Forensic Reasoning]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Image Authenticity and Forensic Reasoning","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Forensic Analysis Assumption.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Forensic Analysis Assumption.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"forensic analysis assumption forensic analysis assumption","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Forensic Analysis Assumption.md","fileName":"Forensic Analysis Assumption.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Forensic Analysis Assumption","heading":"Forensic Analysis Assumption","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A forensic analysis assumption is a condition that must hold for an image test to produce an interpretable result. A geometric method may require identifiable parallel lines, a sensor method may require unsaturated pixels, and a compression method may depend on a particular prior encoding history.\n\nAnalysts must state and test these conditions before interpreting an anomaly. If an assumption is violated, a negative result may be meaningless and a positive result may be a false alarm. Careful application therefore includes judging whether the photograph is suitable for the technique, not merely running the detector.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Image Authenticity and Forensic Reasoning","fakepho